=== docs/install/muse.md ===
<!-- GENERATED by everyharness — edit everyharness.yaml instead -->

# Installing kitchen-sink on muse

## What gets emitted

- \`.muse-plugin/plugin.json\`
- the \`hooks/everyharness\` bootstrap hook (\`session-start\` + \`run-hook.cmd\`)

## Installing

\`\`\`bash
muse plugins install ./
muse plugins approve superpowers
\`\`\`

Or clone and install: \`git clone https://github.com/prime-radiant-inc/everyharness && muse plugins install ./\` + \`muse plugins approve kitchen-sink\`.

Muse registers the \`SessionStart\` bootstrap hook — \`using-kitchen-sink\` (or the generated bootstrap) is injected automatically every session with no per-session opt-in, alongside the other harnesses. Hooks require approval on first install (\`muse plugins approve kitchen-sink\`); skills are active immediately. Restart any active Muse sessions after installing to pick up the hook.

## Caveats

- \`muse plugins install\` validates the plugin — \`muse plugins validate ./\` should report \`valid\` with at most the expected \`multiple-manifests\` warning when the repo also ships other harness manifests.
- Hooks share the \`hooks/everyharness\` directory with Claude Code and Cursor so the three adapters coexist; the \`session-start\` script handles \`MUSE_PLUGIN_ROOT\` with nested \`hookSpecificOutput\` (Muse Spark requires nested, not top-level \`additionalContext\`).

=== docs/install/opencode.md ===
<!-- GENERATED by everyharness — edit everyharness.yaml instead -->

# Installing kitchen-sink on OpenCode

## What gets emitted

- \`package.json\` (shared with the pi adapter when both are active)
- \`.opencode/plugins/kitchen-sink.js\`, the OpenCode plugin module that registers the plugin's skills directory and injects bootstrap context
- a \`.opencode/command/<name>.md\` file for each command (\`ks-hello\`)
- a \`.opencode/agent/<name>.md\` file for each agent (\`ks-reviewer\`)

## Installing

Add the plugin to your project's \`opencode.json\`:

\`\`\`json
{ "plugin": ["kitchen-sink@git+https://github.com/prime-radiant-inc/everyharness.git"] }
\`\`\`

OpenCode loads the plugin module on startup: it registers the skills directory through a config hook (no symlinks needed) and reads commands/agents translated under \`.opencode/\`. Consult the OpenCode plugin docs if this doesn't match your installed version.

## Caveats

- \`package.json\` is generated at the plugin root; if you maintain your own \`package.json\` for this plugin, exclude the opencode and pi adapters from generation (\`harnesses.exclude\`) or merge the fields by hand.

